{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: none.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The program has no model-block sampling statements and no parameters, so the top-level data variables (`theta_l`, `theta_u`, and `delta`) are context inputs rather than protected observations. The program does not use forbidden log-density editing constructs such as `target +=`, `target()`, `reject()`, `fatal_error()`, or `_lp` functions.
","model_safe_stan":"functions {
  real cdf(real x, real mu, real sigma) {
    real denom = sqrt(sigma * x);
    return Phi((x - mu) / denom) - exp(2 * mu / sigma) * Phi(- (x + mu) / denom);
  }

  vector tail_condition(vector y, vector theta, array[] real x_r, array[] int x_i) {
    vector[2] diff;
    if (!is_nan(y[1]) && !is_nan(y[2])) {
      diff[1] = cdf(theta[1], y[1], exp(y[2])) - 0.01;
      diff[2] = cdf(theta[2], y[1], exp(y[2])) - 0.99;
    } else {
      diff[1] = 0;
      diff[2] = 0;
    }
    return diff;
  }
}

data {
  real theta_l;
  real theta_u;
  real delta;
}

transformed data {
  real sigma_guess =
      0.25 * (theta_l + theta_u)
    * (sqrt(1 + 4 * square( (theta_u - theta_l) / (delta * (theta_l + theta_u)) ) ) - 1);
  real mu_guess = 0.5 * (theta_l + theta_u) - sigma_guess;
  vector[2] y_guess = [mu_guess, log(sigma_guess)]';
  vector[2] theta = [theta_l, theta_u]';
  array[0] real x_r;
  array[0] int x_i;

  print("Guesses:");
  print("  mu = ", mu_guess);
  print("  sigma = ", sigma_guess);
}

generated quantities {
  real mu;
  real sigma;
  {
    vector[2] y = algebra_solver(tail_condition, y_guess, theta, x_r, x_i);
    mu = y[1];
    sigma = exp(y[2]);
  }
}
